01:03:48.720 --> 01:03:51.240
What do you know about that girl that you were with in North Shore?

01:03:51.380 --> 01:03:52.060
Money, a liar.

01:03:52.920 --> 01:03:55.300
Just that she works for the people that you're looking for?

01:03:56.080 --> 01:03:59.020
I know. I wasn't watching you up there.

01:03:59.450 --> 01:03:59.970
I was watching...

01:04:00.030 --> 01:04:04.060
All right, look him up.

01:04:04.140 --> 01:04:06.140
Wait a second, what about my ID?

01:04:06.760 --> 01:04:08.460
It's in care of general delivery, I told you.

01:04:08.680 --> 01:04:09.660
Oh, we're working on it.

01:04:09.900 --> 01:04:11.800
Wait a second, what'd you guys give me a break?

01:04:33.320 --> 01:04:37.240
Roth is dead, but Tanner was taken by federal agents before I could get to her.

01:04:43.710 --> 01:04:46.420
He's not dead. Tanner was never programmed.

01:04:48.210 --> 01:04:48.850
It's impossible.

01:04:49.150 --> 01:04:51.630
Is it also impossible that Roth was not even on the yacht?

01:04:52.590 --> 01:04:54.510
And for all we know, not even in the state of Hawaii?

01:04:54.730 --> 01:04:56.130
I saw him kill Roth!

01:04:56.280 --> 01:04:59.960
You saw him fake the killing of another d***.

01:05:01.020 --> 01:05:03.300
Obviously, he got the idea from you.

01:05:09.630 --> 01:05:10.190
What do you suggest?

01:05:11.330 --> 01:05:13.310
I can only assume that since the representatives

01:05:13.310 --> 01:05:14.950
of other countries are already here,

01:05:15.520 --> 01:05:18.900
that Mr. Roth will arrive on time for tomorrow's meeting.

01:05:20.000 --> 01:05:21.900
I shall take care of Mr. Roth.

01:05:23.080 --> 01:05:24.020
You take care of...

01:05:24.780 --> 01:05:27.340
because he can link our faces with our activities.

01:05:28.260 --> 01:05:29.640
We shall leave here tomorrow afternoon.

01:05:30.030 --> 01:05:33.370
having accomplished everything, Mr. Logan.

01:05:35.060 --> 01:05:36.920
You needn't bother coming with us

01:05:38.290 --> 01:05:41.430
unless you have brought the news that Tana is dead.

01:06:03.160 --> 01:06:03.900
Just came through.

01:06:04.080 --> 01:06:09.100
Hello, Dave.

01:06:09.830 --> 01:06:10.350
Hello, Dan.

01:06:10.590 --> 01:06:11.550
What can I do for you?

01:06:12.240 --> 01:06:12.620
What do you mean?

01:06:12.720 --> 01:06:13.320
Didn't he tell you?

01:06:13.780 --> 01:06:16.020
Well, only some minor improprieties,

01:06:16.020 --> 01:06:19.260
like criminal conspiracy, the carrying

01:06:19.260 --> 01:06:20.980
of an unregistered concealed weapon,

01:06:21.160 --> 01:06:23.680
and generally screwing up a high-level operation

01:06:23.680 --> 01:06:25.080
that they have going on over there.

01:06:25.680 --> 01:06:26.340
Dave, come on.

01:06:26.400 --> 01:06:27.520
I need you to vouch for me.

01:06:28.060 --> 01:06:28.900
Oh, I did that.

01:06:29.460 --> 01:06:29.980
I told you.

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:33.000
I told them what they were describing was your normal behavioral pattern.

01:06:33.620 --> 01:06:34.600
This is serious.

01:06:35.260 --> 01:06:38.790
All right, Dad. I talked to them. You're off the hook.

01:06:39.640 --> 01:06:41.040
Let me give you a piece of advice.

01:06:42.120 --> 01:06:45.710
What those guys are working on is pretty heavy, all the way to Washington.

01:06:46.950 --> 01:06:51.100
My suggestion to you is that you cooperate, or they'll have you for lunch.

01:06:51.780 --> 01:06:54.730
I think they already have. Thanks anyway.

01:07:00.920 --> 01:07:01.660
You can go, Tenor.

01:07:03.190 --> 01:07:04.050
How long have you had that?

01:07:04.820 --> 01:07:06.240
Since an hour after we picked you up.

01:07:07.330 --> 01:07:08.510
The ID checks out.

01:07:09.110 --> 01:07:11.860
We just wanted to give you a chance to cool off.

01:07:12.040 --> 01:07:14.100
I guess I was a little overheated.

01:07:15.460 --> 01:07:15.780
Sorry.

01:07:17.060 --> 01:07:17.820
Apologies accepted.

01:07:18.640 --> 01:07:20.360
Look, what would you say if I told you

01:07:20.360 --> 01:07:22.060
I might be able to locate Remick's house?

01:07:22.240 --> 01:07:23.600
Now, remember, I said might.

01:07:24.020 --> 01:07:25.240
Well, I'd say I'd be very interested.

01:07:25.670 --> 01:07:26.350
I'll need a car.

01:07:31.120 --> 01:07:32.280
Stall number six, back lot.

01:07:32.470 --> 01:07:34.890
And if anybody asks, I'll deny I give this back to you.

01:07:35.410 --> 01:07:37.090
I had to sleep in these.

01:07:37.430 --> 01:07:38.610
Think I could get a change of clothes?

01:07:38.860 --> 01:07:40.440
Ask for Charlie in the locker room.

01:07:40.680 --> 01:07:42.000
He's got some kink dolls for you.

01:07:42.960 --> 01:07:43.320
Thanks.

01:07:43.480 --> 01:07:48.520
I wish you were working for us.

01:07:49.460 --> 01:07:50.200
I almost am.

01:09:12.570 --> 01:09:13.510
I know you want to kill me.

01:09:15.940 --> 01:09:16.900
You have every right to.

01:09:17.280 --> 01:09:19.720
Can you come up with one good reason why I shouldn't?

01:09:22.660 --> 01:09:23.340
Why, Lonnie?

01:09:24.460 --> 01:09:25.460
What difference does it make?

01:09:25.560 --> 01:09:26.220
You came here to kill me.

01:09:26.220 --> 01:09:27.580
It makes a big difference to me.

01:09:28.540 --> 01:09:29.600
Now tell me why you did it.

01:09:29.620 --> 01:09:29.980
Because I am.

01:09:30.220 --> 01:09:33.140
If you were in my place, you would have done the same thing.

01:09:33.540 --> 01:09:37.260
Consort with killers, turn your friends over to them.

01:09:37.380 --> 01:09:39.040
It's more complicated than that.

01:09:40.880 --> 01:09:42.300
Do you think it's been easy for me?

01:09:43.080 --> 01:09:47.740
Well, that depends on how much they paid you for your services.

01:09:48.360 --> 01:09:51.320
Oh, thank you, Mr. Tana. I deserve that.

01:09:51.670 --> 01:09:57.020
They pay me a lot, but not in money, in life.

01:10:02.650 --> 01:10:04.410
A lot of people have had their lives threatened

01:10:04.410 --> 01:10:07.090
and still resisted doing what you're doing.

01:10:07.610 --> 01:10:09.850
If they'd have threatened me, I would have resisted.

01:10:16.580 --> 01:10:17.200
Threatened them.

01:10:17.340 --> 01:10:23.470
I was told by Mr. Remick that they'd all be executed

01:10:23.470 --> 01:10:25.270
unless I did exactly as I was told.

01:10:30.120 --> 01:10:31.020
Honey, why didn't you tell me?

01:10:31.080 --> 01:10:31.640
You could have told me.

01:10:31.640 --> 01:10:34.160
There were many times I wanted to help you and tell you.

01:10:34.280 --> 01:10:35.820
I couldn't.

01:10:35.880 --> 01:10:36.880
They were always watching.

01:10:43.750 --> 01:10:48.690
I want you to tell me where Remick's house is.

01:10:48.830 --> 01:10:53.500
No one's watching now.

01:11:02.010 --> 01:11:24.380
being right all the time let's place a part with that magnum get out of here give me the word you

01:11:24.380 --> 01:11:27.200
run ready go

01:11:54.160 --> 01:11:55.560
No, I'll be over in 24 hours.

01:11:56.830 --> 01:11:57.710
Where do your family live?

01:11:58.300 --> 01:11:59.560
The village where I first brought you to.

01:12:01.290 --> 01:12:04.780
Is there some place they can stay and be safe just for 24 hours?

01:12:05.560 --> 01:12:06.180
We leave my grandfather's.

01:12:07.730 --> 01:12:09.520
All right, here's what we're gonna do.

01:12:09.620 --> 01:12:10.880
We're gonna make sure they get off safely.

01:12:11.420 --> 01:12:13.420
Then I want you to tell me where Remick's house is.

01:12:13.900 --> 01:12:16.340
Then we're gonna go to Mr. Fujioka's store and call the police, all right?

01:12:16.460 --> 01:12:18.100
I sure hope you have a dime.

01:12:18.990 --> 01:12:21.150
Let's circle around the other way to the car. I think we lost him.

01:12:41.900 --> 01:12:42.620
Let's get to a phone, huh?

01:12:42.760 --> 01:12:44.220
Oh, there's something important you should know.

01:12:44.890 --> 01:12:46.450
There's a traitor on Mr. Roshad.

01:12:47.550 --> 01:12:47.870
Traitor?

01:12:48.510 --> 01:12:49.730
I heard them talking on the phone.

01:12:49.830 --> 01:12:51.410
He supplies Mr. Remick with information.

01:12:52.070 --> 01:12:53.930
All I know is that his name is Matthews.

01:13:07.870 --> 01:13:08.730
You see anything on your way?

01:13:08.870 --> 01:13:10.430
Nothing, but we blocked off all the streets

01:13:10.430 --> 01:13:11.090
as soon as you called.

01:13:11.820 --> 01:13:12.780
Logan, you think she's going to talk?

01:13:13.050 --> 01:13:13.870
That doesn't matter.

01:13:14.800 --> 01:13:17.930
Even if she tells him where Remick is, he's only one man.

01:13:18.170 --> 01:13:20.240
You just got to be sure he doesn't get to her phone.

01:13:20.400 --> 01:13:21.660
Well, this is an isolated area.

01:13:21.800 --> 01:13:23.160
There's not that many lines running into it.

01:13:23.480 --> 01:13:24.080
Well, cut him.

01:13:24.180 --> 01:13:24.720
Start with that one.

01:13:25.350 --> 01:13:26.410
Send your men on ahead.

01:13:27.760 --> 01:13:28.580
You stay here.

01:13:29.500 --> 01:13:29.960
If 10 or 10, you're going to go ahead.

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:32.340
If he does try to get to a phone, this will be his first logical stop.

01:13:32.910 --> 01:13:33.870
You three, come with me.

01:13:34.070 --> 01:13:35.210
And if he happens to come by here?

01:13:36.300 --> 01:13:36.780
Kill him.

01:14:21.950 --> 01:14:26.500
I think Logan Beda's here. The man's waiting for us.

01:14:27.880 --> 01:14:29.700
The next village is only two miles from here.

01:14:30.760 --> 01:14:31.700
No, that's too close.

01:14:32.270 --> 01:14:34.270
I'm sure they got everything on the shoreline covered.

01:14:34.910 --> 01:14:36.410
If I were them, I'd cut the phone lines.

01:14:37.440 --> 01:14:38.100
What about inland?

01:14:39.680 --> 01:14:41.420
Cooney, it's about 20 miles from here.

01:14:42.560 --> 01:14:43.060
Want to navigate?

01:14:43.300 --> 01:14:43.500
Yeah.

01:15:08.120 --> 01:15:09.040
Uh oh. Trouble.

01:15:49.260 --> 01:15:49.700
Jump ahead.

01:16:02.110 --> 01:16:02.190
Thank you.

01:17:30.120 --> 01:17:30.460
Thank you.

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:01.540
phone at the pineapple factory. Come on.

01:19:00.060 --> 01:19:02.880
This is a collect call from Dantana to Lieutenant Luke Keechee.

01:19:05.480 --> 01:19:06.160
Luke, it's me.

01:19:06.320 --> 01:19:07.820
I got the location at Remick's house.

01:19:08.020 --> 01:19:08.380
How?

01:19:10.750 --> 01:19:12.090
I thought she was tied with Remick.

01:19:12.330 --> 01:19:13.350
She was coerced.

01:19:41.100 --> 01:19:43.430
Well, where is the house?

01:19:43.590 --> 01:19:45.980
She describes it as the old Waimini estate.

01:19:46.290 --> 01:19:49.440
Figures been buried under layers of legal papers

01:19:49.440 --> 01:19:51.480
belonging to a foreign cooperation for years.

01:19:51.680 --> 01:19:56.010
Where are you calling from?

01:19:56.380 --> 01:19:58.380
From an old pineapple factory near Kunia.

01:19:58.520 --> 01:19:59.140
Sit tight.

01:19:59.390 --> 01:19:59.970
We'll see you there.

01:20:00.820 --> 01:20:03.800
One other thing, Remick has a pipeline to Roth's yacht.

01:20:03.980 --> 01:20:05.080
His name is Matthews.

01:20:09.240 --> 01:20:23.150
You've embarrassed me, Mr. Tanner.

01:20:24.230 --> 01:20:27.570
I don't like that. You're gonna pay for it now.

01:20:30.160 --> 01:20:38.830
your bullets mr tanner you fired six remember question would you have carried extra ammunition

01:20:38.830 --> 01:20:49.770
on your way to see the girl i think not i'm betting my life on it

01:21:03.480 --> 01:21:05.860
You come from a gambling city, Mr. Tanner.

01:21:06.080 --> 01:21:07.000
Will you take my bet?

01:21:23.090 --> 01:21:23.350
What?

01:21:24.120 --> 01:21:26.420
Run or I'll blow you away just for the hell of it.

01:21:27.230 --> 01:21:27.630
Run where?

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:30.280
There.

01:21:45.440 --> 01:21:46.140
Dr. Ribbons!

01:21:46.600 --> 01:21:46.960
Really?

01:21:48.580 --> 01:21:49.160
Show me.

01:21:50.620 --> 01:21:52.660
Would you rather have your brain spread around?

01:21:54.840 --> 01:21:56.760
There's a service road 50 yards ahead.

01:21:58.120 --> 01:21:58.760
You make it.

01:22:00.000 --> 01:22:00.960
I might let you live.

01:22:03.280 --> 01:22:03.700
Run.

01:23:02.140 --> 01:23:11.580
You're not a fool, Tanner. You may get inside those walls, but Remick will see that you never get out of them alive.

01:23:25.590 --> 01:23:29.920
I watched you gun down an old man in cold blood. The most senseless killer.

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:35.350
imaginable. I watched you murder a young girl whose only crime was protecting her

01:23:35.350 --> 01:23:40.700
family. Then I came down to your level. I wanted to see you bleed to death in that

01:23:40.700 --> 01:23:45.760
field, but you got lucky, Logan, so don't push that luck.

01:25:41.260 --> 01:25:46.030
See, Mr. Tanner, you have not escaped me, after all.

01:25:46.620 --> 01:25:49.320
I didn't come here to escape from you, Remick!

01:25:53.680 --> 01:25:59.980
Very courageous, and so like you, to walk back into the lion's...

01:26:00.000 --> 01:26:17.030
lair alone in the short time i've had the pleasure of your acquaintance i have made a rather detailed

01:26:17.030 --> 01:26:27.530
study of your character fascinating fascinating well why don't you tell me about it it's here

01:26:32.360 --> 01:26:35.310
Could it be the death of the girl?

01:26:35.510 --> 01:26:37.150
Am I correct, Mr. Tanner?

01:26:38.430 --> 01:26:39.550
Is the girl dead?

01:26:41.550 --> 01:26:42.210
She's dead.

01:26:43.830 --> 01:26:46.890
Mr. Logan finally managed to do something right.

01:26:48.300 --> 01:26:49.640
I should congratulate him,

01:26:51.160 --> 01:26:54.060
but obviously your presence here means that I should not be able to do so.

01:26:55.270 --> 01:26:57.000
Did you kill him?

01:26:58.280 --> 01:26:59.770
No, kill!

01:27:00.830 --> 01:27:02.750
But I came close, Remick.

01:27:02.970 --> 01:27:05.550
Close? Pity.

01:27:06.880 --> 01:27:08.500
Now I shall have to do it myself.

01:27:09.050 --> 01:27:10.550
Is that a part of your game?

01:27:13.310 --> 01:27:13.710
Exactly.

01:27:14.390 --> 01:27:16.170
Oh, I shall miss you, Mr. Tanner.

01:27:16.350 --> 01:27:17.510
I shall miss you very much.

01:27:19.560 --> 01:27:21.870
Never had so worthy an adversary.

01:27:22.660 --> 01:27:25.370
And I do very much.

01:27:27.900 --> 01:27:29.640
And so I shall give you a choice, Mr. Tanner.

01:27:31.600 --> 01:27:36.890
Tell me, in what manner do you prefer to die?

01:28:01.690 --> 01:28:26.150
you got everybody but him yeah what you got in mind he'll know where Remick is

01:28:26.840 --> 01:28:29.760
okay but I don't want him back in sections

01:28:30.320 --> 01:28:30.980
Come on, friend.

01:28:31.180 --> 01:28:38.580
I'm going to ask you one simple question.

01:28:38.780 --> 01:28:40.680
And either you give me a straight answer,

01:28:40.700 --> 01:28:41.960
or you're going to go home in a sack.

01:28:42.900 --> 01:28:43.620
Where's Remick?

01:28:45.990 --> 01:28:46.590
I don't know.

01:28:48.720 --> 01:28:49.820
Get it together, friend.

01:28:50.560 --> 01:28:51.380
Where's Remick?

01:28:52.320 --> 01:28:53.320
He's meeting the ship.

01:28:53.930 --> 01:28:54.510
What ship?

01:28:56.450 --> 01:28:57.110
What ship?

01:28:57.460 --> 01:28:58.560
The Matsu, man.

01:29:00.000 --> 01:29:01.460
It's anchored out in the international waters.

01:29:02.290 --> 01:29:03.330
Behind Wamanalo Bay.

01:29:04.920 --> 01:29:05.540
Let's go.

01:29:31.340 --> 01:29:32.200
Today's your walkie-talkie.

01:29:33.640 --> 01:29:34.740
Hello, I'm the chopper pilot.

01:29:34.960 --> 01:29:35.420
This is Tanner.

01:29:36.320 --> 01:29:37.600
Can you come down and give me a lift?

01:29:41.140 --> 01:29:42.620
I'll come down on the clearing out front.

01:33:02.840 --> 01:33:05.400
Dan, how did you fool him into thinking that you were brainwashed?

01:33:05.560 --> 01:33:07.360
Well, that was easy. I blew up a guy.

01:33:08.530 --> 01:33:09.350
That'd fool me.

01:33:10.480 --> 01:33:12.760
Binz, it was rigged. Phony bullet, phony victim.

01:33:13.160 --> 01:33:15.100
They had to test me to make sure I'd go through with it.

01:33:15.600 --> 01:33:18.020
I still can't believe horrible things like that really happened.

01:33:18.950 --> 01:33:21.450
I wonder how I'd react if somebody tried to brainwash me.

01:33:22.670 --> 01:33:24.230
Before or after you stopped crying.

01:33:25.740 --> 01:33:26.640
Think that's funny?

01:33:28.130 --> 01:33:29.490
No, that is not funny, Binz.

01:33:30.060 --> 01:33:31.520
Well, anyway, welcome back, Dan.

01:33:32.100 --> 01:33:33.380
I know how I'd handle it.

01:33:34.120 --> 01:33:37.710
I just keep saying to myself, what would Burt Reynolds do?

01:33:40.700 --> 01:33:42.360
I'm sure you don't know. Thank you very much.

01:34:00.000 --> 01:34:00.180
You
